                "reply_count": 433,
                "retweet_count": 1914,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Your claim that \"not one federal dollar\" goes to undocumented immigrants overlooks emergency Medicaid, which uses federal funds for acute care\u2014 hundreds of millions annually. States like CA also use state funds (often tied to federal block grants) for non-emergency care, a loophole needing closure. Thats why BBB language is needed/Trumps EO. \n\nYour 17M Americans \"kicked off\" figure ignores a lot, to include THEY ARE eligible if they comply with work requirements (80 hrs/month, including volunteering) specifically ref. able-bodied adults 19-64. It\u2019s not \"forcing\" work but incentivizing it, per Clinton-era reforms. GOP Senators\u2019 admissions reflect policy trade-offs, not a conspiracy. \n\nAmericans, not just Floridians, deserve clarity, not spin. I am happy to have this debate with you in a respectful fashion that can provide that to the American people.",
